course: dictionary
lesson: 1124
title: Breakfast in context
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Breakfast usually means the first meal of the day, eaten in the morning. In «Breakfast takes 20 minutes and washing and dressing take 25 minutes, so he must get up by 7:00», it means the meal itself, and the sentence tells you it takes time.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. In «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast», breakfast is a time and a place, like sitting at the table in the morning. Try your meaning in the sentence: "says sorry at the first meal of the day" still makes sense.
explain: Breakfast can also be a verb, but this is rare. «The sign of “The Red Lion” reminds him “that he had not breakfasted that day”» means he had not eaten breakfast. You will mostly meet this old or formal use in older books.
explain: Breakfast also appears in phrases such as have breakfast, for breakfast, breakfast club and bed and breakfast. Each phrase has its own meaning, so read the words around it to find out which one is being used.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Breakfast means the first meal of the day, eaten in the morning.
fact: To breakfast means to eat breakfast; it is old or formal and rare.
fact: Breakfast gives your body and brain energy after the night, which helps you concentrate at school.
fact: Breakfasts differ around the world: a full English breakfast, pancakes in the USA, porridge, and Vegemite on toast in Australia.
exercise: «Breakfast takes 20 minutes and washing and dressing take 25 minutes.» What is breakfast in this sentence? | A game played before school | A shop where you buy bread | A morning walk | *The first meal of the day, eaten in the morning
exercise: «He lies awake feeling awful and says sorry at breakfast.» Find and copy one word that means not asleep. | breakfast | awful | feeling | *awake
exercise: Some schools run breakfast clubs. What is a breakfast club? | *A place or group where children can eat breakfast, often at school | A club that sells shoes | A club for people who cook at night | A club for baking cakes at home
test: «The sign of “The Red Lion” reminds him “that he had not breakfasted that day”.» What does breakfasted mean here? | Had a long walk | *Had eaten breakfast | Had gone to sleep early | Had bought a new coat
test: In the phrase bed and breakfast, what does breakfast mean? | A breakfast fair | A type of bread | *A place to stay where breakfast is included | A cold drink at night
exam: Based on the lesson, which sentence best explains breakfast? | Breakfast is a type of game | Breakfast is only eaten at night | *Breakfast is the first meal of the day, eaten in the morning, which gives your body energy | Breakfast is a kind of school bell
